<worksheet>
<title>Phase portraits for linear systems with Complex  eigenvalues</title>
<objectives>
<ul>
            <li>Phase portraits for linear systems with a Complex eigenvalue with a positive real part.</li>
            
                <li>Phase portraits for linear systems with a Complex eigenvalue with a negative real part.</li>
                    <li>
                        <p>
                            Phase portraits for linear systems with a Complex eigenvalue with a zero real part.
                        </p>
                    </li>
        </ul>    
</objectives>
<introduction>
    <p>
        In this worksheet we will discuss the cases of the phase portraits for the linear
                system
                <md>
                    \frac{d\vec{Y}}{dt}=A\vec{Y}
                </md>
                where <m>A</m> is a <m>2\times 2</m> matrix over <m>\mathbb{R}</m>, where the eigenvalues of <m>A</m> are complex, i.e. <m>\lambda=\alpha\pm\beta i</m>.
    </p>
</introduction>
</worksheet>